  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Indore Municipal Corporation vs Sudhanshu on 26 March, 2026 Neutral Citation No. 2026:Mphc-Ind:8209 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Rajendra Kumar Vani On The 26th Of March, 2026 Criminal Appeal No. 3128 of 2024 Indore Municipal Corporation Versus Sudhanshu Appearance: Shri Madhav Lahoti - Advocate for the appellant. Order 1.",
    "facts": "This appeal has been filed under Section 419 of BNSS, 2023 (378 (4) of Cr.P.C.) by \"victim\" against judgment dated 31.10.2023 passed by Special Judicial Magistrate, Food Adulteration Act and Judicial Magistrate First Class, Indore (M.P.) in Criminal Case No.2614851/2009, whereby respondent/accused has been acquitted of an offence under Section 7(i)(ii)(v) read with Section 16(1)(a)(i), 16(1)(a)(ii) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. 2. Aforesaid criminal case was instituted on the basis of private complaint filed by the victim/appellant. Present case is arising out of the judgment dated 31.10.2023 passed by Special Judicial Magistrate, Food Adulteration Act and Judicial Magistrate First Class, Indore, whereby judgment of acquittal has been passed.",
    "arguments": "The aforesaid issue is no longer res integra in light of the judgment of Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Celestium Financial Vs. A. NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-IND:8209 2 CRA-3128-2024 Gnanasekaran Etc., 2025 SCC Online SC 1320. Since the case was based on private complaint and judgment of acquittal has been passed, therefore, the dictum passed by Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Celestium Indore Municipal Corporation vs Sudhanshu on 26 March, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/194524678/ 1 Financial (supra) would apply. 6. It is observed by Hon'ble Apex Court in para 9 and 10 of Celestium Financial (supra) as under:- \"9.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The aforesaid issue is no longer res integra in light of the judgment of Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Celestium Financial Vs. A. NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-IND:8209 2 CRA-3128-2024 Gnanasekaran Etc., 2025 SCC Online SC 1320. Since the case was based on private complaint and judgment of acquittal has been passed, therefore, the dictum passed by Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Celestium Indore Municipal Corporation vs Sudhanshu on 26 March, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/194524678/ 1 Financial (supra) would apply. 6. It is observed by Hon'ble Apex Court in para 9 and 10 of Celestium Financial (supra) as under:- \"9."
  },
